hadiths[241]{hadithnumber,text}:
"6742","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""This fire of yours, which the children of Adam kindle, is one part of seventy parts of the fire of Hell."" It was said: ""O Messenger of Allah! Was this not sufficient?"" He (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""It has been made to exceed it by sixty-nine (69) parts, each part of them as hot as this (worldly fire)."""
"6743","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""This fire of yours is one part of seventy parts of the fire of Hell; each part of it has heat equal to this (worldly fire)."""
"6744","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Some people of my Ummah were shown to me as fighters in the path of Allah, riding upon the waves of this sea like kings seated upon thrones."""
"6745","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""We shall begin with that with which Allah began."""
"6746","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The first people of this Ummah were saved through certainty and abstinence (zuhd), and its last people will be destroyed through miserliness and long hopes."""
"6747","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Remove harmful things from the path of the Muslims."""
"6748","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""I have sacrificed here, and the whole of Mina is a place of sacrifice, so sacrifice at your own camps. I stood here, and the whole plain of Arafah is a place of standing; and I stood here as well, and the whole of Muzdalifah (Jam') is a place of standing."""
"6749","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""We are the last of the nations and the first to be brought to account. It will be said: 'Where is the unlettered nation and its Prophet?' So we are the last (in time) yet the first (in rank)."""
"6750","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""We are more entitled to doubt than Ibrahim (peace be upon him), when he said: 'My Lord! Show me how You give life to the dead.' Allah said: 'Do you not believe?' He said: 'Yes indeed! But so that my heart may be at rest.' And may Allah have mercy on Lut (peace be upon him); he was indeed taking refuge in a mighty support. And had I remained in prison as long as Yusuf (peace be upon him) remained, I would have responded to the one who summoned me at once."""
"6751","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""We are more entitled to Musa (peace be upon him) and closer to him than you."""
"6752","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""We are the last in coming into the world, yet we will be the foremost on the Day of Resurrection, except that they were given the Book before us and we were given it after them. Then this day (Friday) is the one that Allah made obligatory upon them, but they differed about it, and Allah guided us to it. So in this matter the people follow us: the Jews tomorrow and the Christians the day after tomorrow."""
"6753","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""We are Banu al-Nadr bin Kinanah; we do not disown our mother, nor do we dissociate ourselves from our father."""
"6754","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Tomorrow we shall camp at Khayf Bani Kinanah, where Quraysh swore an alliance upon disbelief."""
"6755","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""A man who had never done any good deed removed a thorny branch from the path: either it was on a felled tree and he threw it away, or it had been lying there and he moved it off the path. So Allah accepted this good deed of his and admitted him into Paradise."""
"6756","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The Black Stone (al-Hajar al-Aswad) came down from Paradise, and it was whiter than milk; then the sins of the children of Adam turned it black."""
"6757","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Jibril (peace be upon him) came down and led me in prayer. So I prayed with him, then I prayed with him, then I prayed with him, then I prayed with him, then I prayed with him. Then he said: 'It is with this very timing that I have been commanded.'"""
"6758","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""An angel came down from the sky and refuted what he had said to you. Then, when you defended yourself, Shaytan came in, and I do not sit where Shaytan has come."""
"6759","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""A prophet from among the prophets camped beneath a tree, and an ant bit him. He gave an order and his belongings were taken out from beneath it; then he gave an order and its nest was burned with fire. So Allah Almighty revealed to him: 'Would it not have sufficed to punish just one ant?'"""
"6760","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""This verse was revealed concerning the people of Quba: 'In it are men who love to purify themselves, and Allah loves those who purify themselves.'"""
"6761","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""We will be patient and we will not retaliate."""
"6762","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""I was granted victory by the saba (the east wind), and the people of Ad were destroyed by the dabur (the west wind)."""
"6763","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""May Allah make radiant the person who hears a hadith from us and memorises it until he conveys it to someone else, for often a bearer of knowledge conveys it to one who has more understanding than himself, and often a bearer of knowledge is not himself one of understanding."""
"6764","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""May Allah make radiant the person who hears something from us and conveys it just as he heard it, for often the one to whom it is conveyed retains it better than the one who heard it."""
"6765","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""May Allah make radiant the servant who heard my words, retained them, then conveyed them on my behalf, for often a bearer of knowledge is not himself one of understanding, and often a bearer of knowledge conveys it to one who has more understanding than himself."""
"6766","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""May Allah make radiant the servant who heard my words, retained them and preserved them, then conveyed them to one who had not heard them, for often a bearer of knowledge is not himself one of understanding, and often a bearer of knowledge conveys it to one who has more understanding than himself. There are three things concerning which the heart of a Muslim does not harbour rancour: making one's deeds sincerely for Allah, giving sincere counsel to the rulers of the Muslims, and holding fast to their community, for their supplication (and unity) encompasses those behind them."""
"6767","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The man's fluid is white and thick, and the woman's fluid is yellow and thin; whichever of the two prevails, the resemblance is to that one."""
"6768","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""What an excellent condiment vinegar is!"""
"6769","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""What an excellent jihad Hajj is!"""
"6770","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""What an excellent man Abu Bakr is! What an excellent man Umar is! What an excellent man Abu Ubaydah bin al-Jarrah is! What an excellent man Usayd bin Hudayr is! What an excellent man Thabit bin Qays bin Shammas is! What an excellent man Mu'adh bin Jabal is! What an excellent man Mu'adh bin Amr bin al-Jamuh is! What an excellent man Suhayl bin Bayda is!"""
"6771","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""What an excellent man Abdullah is! If only he would offer the night prayer (tahajjud)."""
"6772","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""What an excellent pre-dawn meal (suhur) dates are!"""
"6773","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""How excellent are these two surahs which are recited in the two rak'ahs before Fajr: Surah al-Kafirun and Surah al-Ikhlas."""
"6774","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""What an excellent charity it is to lend a milch she-camel, and what an excellent charity too to lend a milch goat: she goes out in the morning with a vessel (of milk) and returns in the evening with a vessel."""
"6775","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""What an excellent death it is for a man to die defending his right!"""
"6776","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""What an excellent servant of Allah Khalid bin al-Walid is! He is one of the swords of Allah."""
"6777","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""How excellent it is for a slave who worships his Lord well and is sincere towards his master, and dies in that state; how excellent it is for him!"""
"6778","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""There are two blessings in which most people are at a loss: health and free time."""
"6779","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The soul of the believer remains held back because of his debt until his debt is paid off."""
"6780","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""A man's spending on his family is charity."""
"6781","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""We will fulfil the covenant made with them, and we will seek Allah's help against them."""
"6782","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Two rivers are from Paradise: the Nile and the Euphrates."""
"6783","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""I have been forbidden from walking naked."""
"6784","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""I have been forbidden from nakedness."""
"6785","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""I have been forbidden (from harming) those who pray."""
"6786","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""I had forbidden you from certain vessels, yet vessels neither make anything lawful nor make it unlawful, and every intoxicant is unlawful."""
"6787","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""I had forbidden you from making nabidh in anything other than a waterskin; so now drink from waterskins of every kind, but do not drink anything intoxicating."""
"6788","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""I had forbidden you from three things, and now I command you regarding them. I had forbidden you from visiting graves; so now visit them, for in visiting them there is a reminder. And I had forbidden you, concerning drinks, from drinking in anything other than leather vessels; so now drink from every vessel, except that you must not drink anything intoxicating. And I had forbidden you from eating the meat of sacrificial animals after three days; so now eat it and benefit from it on your journeys."""
"6789","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""I had forbidden you from visiting graves; so now visit them, for in them there is a lesson for you."""
"6790","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""I had forbidden you from visiting graves; so now visit them, for it reminds you of death."""
"6791","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""We were forbidden from speaking during prayer, except with the Qur'an and remembrance (dhikr)."""
"6792","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The wailing woman, if she does not repent before her death, will be raised on the Day of Resurrection wearing a garment of tar and a shirt of scabies."""
"6793","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Damage caused by fire carries no liability (no compensation is due)."""
"6794","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Fire is an enemy, so beware of it."""
"6795","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""People follow Quraysh in good and in evil."""
"6796","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""People are like mines (of minerals); those who were the best of them in the Days of Ignorance are the best of them in Islam, provided they gain understanding of the religion. People follow Quraysh in this matter: their Muslims follow their Muslims, and their disbelievers follow their disbelievers. You will find among the best of people the one who most dislikes this matter, until he becomes involved in it."""
"6797","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""People are like mines, like mines of gold and silver; those who were the best of them in the Days of Ignorance are the best of them in Islam, provided they gain understanding. And souls are like enlisted troops: those of them that recognise one another come together, and those that are strangers to one another differ."""
"6798","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""People are the children of Adam (peace be upon him), and Adam was created from dust."""
"6799","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""A Prophet is not inherited from."""
"6800","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The stars are a source of safety for the sky; when the stars go, there will come to the sky what it has been promised. And I am a source of safety for my Companions; when I go, there will come to my Companions what they have been promised. And my Companions are a source of safety for my Ummah; when my Companions go, there will come to my Ummah what it has been promised."""
"6801","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Spitting phlegm in the mosque is a sin, and its expiation is burying it."""
"6802","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Remorse is repentance."""
"6803","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Remorse is repentance, and the one who repents from a sin is like one who has committed no sin at all."""
"6804","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Vows are of two kinds: a vow made in obedience to Allah is for Allah, and it must be fulfilled; and a vow made in disobedience to Allah is for Satan, and it should not be fulfilled, and its expiation is the same as the expiation for an oath."""
"6805","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""A vow: its expiation is like the expiation for an oath."""
"6806","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Help comes with patience, and relief comes with hardship, and indeed with hardship there is ease."""
"6807","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Marriage is my Sunnah, so whoever does not act upon my Sunnah is not of me. And marry, for I will take pride in your great numbers before the other nations on the Day of Resurrection. Whoever has the means, let him marry, and whoever does not have the means, let him fast, for fasting is a shield for him."""
"6808","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Sleep is the brother of death, and the people of Paradise do not die."""
"6809","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Wailing over the dead is one of the practices of the Days of Ignorance, and the wailing woman, if she does not repent before she dies, will be raised on the Day of Resurrection wearing garments of tar, then she will be scorched in shirts of the flames of the Fire."""
"6810","The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) forbade that a woman who wails and laments loudly should accompany a funeral."
"6811","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) forbade covering walls with curtains."
"6812","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) forbade tying up an animal and making it a target."
"6813","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) forbade speaking to women without the permission of their husbands."
"6814","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) forbade urinating in still water."
"6815","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) forbade a man urinating in the place where he bathes."
"6816","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) forbade people vying in pride with one another over the building and adornment of mosques."
"6817","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) forbade making any living thing a target for shooting."
"6818","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) forbade a man using saffron colour or scent."
"6819","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) forbade handing a naked sword (drawn from its sheath) from hand to hand."
"6820","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) forbade breathing into a vessel or blowing into it."
"6821","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) forbade a man sitting between two men without their permission."
"6822","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) forbade a man sitting in prayer while leaning on his left hand, and he said: ""This is the way the Jews pray."""
"6823","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) forbade sitting between the sun and the shade, and he said: ""It is the sitting place of Satan."""
"6824","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) forbade anyone combining his name and his kunyah."
"6825","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) forbade taking the Qur'an into the land of the enemy."
"6826","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) forbade anyone cleaning himself after relieving himself (istinja) with a bone, dung or charcoal."
"6827","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) forbade cleaning oneself after relieving oneself (istinja) with dried dung or a bone."
"6828","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) forbade giving four names: Aflah, Yasar, Nafi' and Rabah."
"6829","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) forbade a man drinking water while standing."
"6830","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) forbade a man praying in a sheet that he has not wrapped over his shoulders, and he forbade a man praying in trousers alone without an upper wrap."
"6831","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) forbade a man praying while his hair is tied back."
"6832","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) forbade a man praying while holding back urine."
"6833","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) forbade praying behind one who is talking or one who is sleeping."
"6834","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) forbade praying the funeral prayer among the graves."
"6835","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) forbade a man lying on his back and placing one leg over the other."
"6836","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) forbade a man coming to his family suddenly at night."
"6837","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) forbade singling out Friday alone for fasting."
"6838","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) forbade a man being made to get up from his seat so that another may sit in it."
"6839","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) forbade killing any animal by tying it up and making it suffer."
"6840","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) forbade a man sitting between the shade and the sun."
"6841","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) forbade sitting on a grave, and plastering it or building upon it."
"6842","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) forbade the imam standing on a raised place while the people behind him are on lower ground."
"6843","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) forbade writing anything on a grave."
"6844","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) forbade a man touching his private part with his right hand, walking in one shoe, wrapping a single garment around his whole body without leaving the hands free, and sitting with his knees drawn up and bound in a single garment that leaves his private part exposed."
"6845","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) forbade walking in one shoe or one leather sock."
"6846","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) forbade withholding the surplus water of a well from others."
"6847","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) forbade a man sleeping on a roof that has no parapet around it."
"6848","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) forbade a man putting on his shoes while standing."
"6849","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) forbade blowing into a drink, and drinking from the chipped edge of a cup or from the side of its handle."
"6850","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) forbade blowing into food and drink."
"6851","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) forbade bending back the mouths of waterskins and drinking directly from them."
"6852","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) forbade eating onions."
"6853","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) forbade eating onions, leeks and garlic."
"6854","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) forbade eating garlic."
"6855","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) forbade consuming the meat and milk of the jallalah (an animal that feeds on filth)."
"6856","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) forbade eating the meat of the dabb (a kind of lizard)."
"6857","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) forbade eating the meat of the mujaththamah (an animal that is tied up and made a target for arrows)."
"6858","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) forbade eating the meat of every beast of prey that has fangs."
"6859","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) forbade eating the meat of every beast of prey that has fangs, and eating the meat of every bird that has talons."
"6860","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) forbade eating the meat of domestic donkeys."
"6861","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) forbade placing the hands on the hips during the prayer."
"6862","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) forbade castration."
"6863","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) forbade eating two dates together at a time, unless a man asks permission from his companion."
"6864","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) forbade iq'a' (sitting on both heels like a dog) in the prayer."
"6865","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) forbade iq'a' and tawarruk in the prayer."
"6866","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) forbade eating and drinking from vessels of gold and silver."
"6867","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) forbade tabattul (abandoning marriage to devote oneself entirely to worship)."
"6868","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) forbade tabaqqur (amassing and spreading out wealth excessively) in wealth."
"6869","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) forbade wearing a gold ring."
"6870","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) forbade combing the hair except every other day."
"6871","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) forbade going to excessive lengths (burdening oneself to make arrangements) for a guest."
"6872","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) forbade picking dates at night and harvesting crops at night."
"6873","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) forbade disputing about the Qur'an."
"6874","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) forbade sitting at a dining spread at which wine is being drunk, and a man eating while lying on his stomach."
"6875","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) forbade riding the jallalah (an animal that feeds on filth) or drinking its milk."
"6876","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) forbade sitting with the knees drawn up and bound on the day of Jumu'ah while the imam is delivering the sermon."
"6877","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) forbade flicking pebbles, and he said: ""It neither kills game nor harms the enemy; rather, it gouges out the eye and breaks the tooth."""
"6878","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) forbade using impure (unlawful) medicine."
"6879","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) forbade using dibaj (brocade), silk and istabraq (thick silk cloth)."
"6880","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) forbade incantations (unlawful charms), amulets and tiwalah (magic to induce love)."
"6881","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) forbade riding on leopard skins."
"6882","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) forbade falsehood and false testimony."
"6883","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) forbade letting the garment hang down in the prayer, and a man covering his mouth."
"6884","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) forbade slaughtering milk-giving animals."
"6885","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) forbade buying and selling in the mosque, announcing a lost item in it, and reciting poetry in it; and he forbade sitting in circles before the prayer on the day of Jumu'ah."
"6886","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) forbade drinking from vessels of gold and silver, wearing gold and silk, and riding on leopard skins."
"6887","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) forbade drinking water while standing."
"6888","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) forbade drinking from the chipped edge of a cup, and blowing into a drink."
"6889","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) forbade drinking directly from the mouth of a waterskin."
"6890","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) forbade drinking directly from the mouth of a waterskin, riding the jallalah, and the mujaththamah."
"6891","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) forbade shighar (marrying by exchanging women without a dowry)."
"6892","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) forbade praying after Fajr until the sun rises, and after Asr until the sun sets."
"6893","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) forbade praying facing towards graves."
"6894","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) forbade wrapping the whole body in a single garment, and sitting with the knees drawn up and bound in a single garment."
"6895","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) forbade making images."
"6896","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) forbade laughing at breaking wind."
"6897","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) forbade treatment by cauterisation."
"6898","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) forbade mut'ah (temporary marriage)."
"6899","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) forbade muthlah (mutilating the limbs of a corpse)."
"6900","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) forbade muhaqalah, mukhasarah, mulamasah, munabadhah and muzabanah."
"6901","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) forbade mukhabarah (giving land for cultivation in return for a share of its produce)."
"6902","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) forbade muzabanah (selling fresh dates for dried dates by estimation)."
"6903","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) forbade muzabanah and muhaqalah."
"6904","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) forbade muzara'ah."
"6905","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) forbade wearing clothes dyed deep red."
"6906","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) forbade munabadhah and mulamasah."
"6907","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) forbade using red saddle-cushions and qassi (cloth mixed with silk)."
"6908","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) forbade using purple (red-coloured) saddle-cushions."
"6909","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) forbade najsh (raising the bid by way of deception)."
"6910","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) forbade making vows."
"6911","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) forbade na'i (publicly announcing a death)."
"6912","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) forbade blowing into a drink."
"6913","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) forbade blowing into food and drink."
"6914","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) forbade wailing, pictures, the skins of predatory animals, immodest display (of women), singing, gold, khazz (cloth mixed with silk) and silk."
"6915","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) forbade sleeping before Isha and talking after it."
"6916","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) forbade wailing."
"6917","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) forbade plundering and muthlah."
"6918","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) forbade plundering and snatching."
"6919","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) forbade solitude, that is, a man spending the night alone."
"6920","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) forbade branding the face and striking the face."
"6921","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) forbade tattooing."
"6922","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) forbade wisal (joining fasts without breaking the fast in between)."
"6923","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) forbade selling fruits until they are safe from blight."
"6924","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) forbade selling fruits until their ripeness becomes evident and they are safe from blight."
"6925","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) forbade selling fresh fruit for dried fruit (dates)."
"6926","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) forbade selling fresh fruit for dried dates by measure, selling grapes for raisins by measure, and selling a standing crop for wheat by measure."
"6927","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) forbade selling fruit until it ripens and becomes good."
"6928","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) forbade selling fruit until its ripeness becomes evident, and he forbade selling the fruit of date-palms until it changes colour."
"6929","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) forbade transactions made by throwing a pebble, and transactions involving deception."
"6930","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) forbade selling an animal for an animal on credit."
"6931","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) forbade selling gold for silver on credit."
"6932","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) forbade selling several years' fruit in advance."
"6933","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) forbade selling a live goat for meat."
"6934","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) forbade selling a heap of dates whose quantity is not known for a specified measure of dates."
"6935","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) forbade selling grain onwards until it has been measured twice, so that any excess goes to its owner and any shortfall is borne by him too."
"6936","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) forbade selling meat for a live animal."
"6937","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) forbade transactions in madamin (the young in the wombs of female animals), malaqih (the progeny of male animals) and habal al-habalah (until the birth of the offspring of the young in a she-camel's womb)."
"6938","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) forbade selling the fruit of date-palms until it changes colour, and he forbade selling ears of grain until they turn white and are safe from blight."
"6939","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) forbade selling wala' (the right of inheritance from a freed slave) and giving it away as a gift."
"6940","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) forbade transactions in habal al-habalah."
"6941","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) forbade taking a fee for a camel's stud service, and selling water and land for cultivation."
"6942","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) forbade selling surplus water."
"6943","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) forbade making two deals in one deal."
"6944","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) forbade buying trade goods on the way before they reach the market."
"6945","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) forbade buying goods and animals coming from outside on the way before they reach the market."
"6946","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) forbade taking or giving the price of a dog, except a hunting dog."
"6947","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) forbade the price of a dog, except a trained dog."
"6948","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) forbade the price of a dog, the price of swine, the price of wine, the earnings of prostitution, and the fee for a male animal's stud service."
"6949","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) forbade the price of a dog, the fee for blood (cupping), and the earnings of prostitution."
"6950","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) forbade the price of a dog and the price of a cat."
"6951","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) forbade the price of a dog, the earnings of prostitution, and the fee of a soothsayer."
"6952","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) forbade carrying out the lashes of a prescribed punishment (hadd) in the mosques."
"6953","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) forbade using the skins of predatory animals."
"6954","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) forbade the gold ring."
"6955","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) forbade the gold ring and the iron ring."
"6956","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) forbade castrating horses and animals."
"6957","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) forbade riding on leopard skins."
"6958","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) forbade reviling the dead."
"6959","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) forbade combining a loan with a sale, stipulating two conditions in one sale, selling something that you do not have, and earning profit on something for which you have not borne the liability."
"6960","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) forbade tying up a living creature to torment it, and castrating animals."
"6961","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) forbade fasting on six days of the year: the three days of Tashriq, the day of Eid al-Fitr, the day of Eid al-Adha, and singling out Friday alone from among the other days."
"6962","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) forbade fasting on the day of Eid al-Fitr and the day of sacrifice."
"6963","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) forbade fasting on Friday."
"6964","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) forbade fasting one day before Ramadan, and fasting on Eid al-Adha, Eid al-Fitr and the days of Tashriq."
"6965","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) forbade eating food prepared by people competing to boast over one another."
"6966","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) forbade the fee for a male animal's stud service."
"6967","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) forbade the fee for a male animal's stud service, and paying the miller from the flour he has ground."
"6968","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) forbade killing four creatures: the ant, the honeybee, the hoopoe and the shrike."
"6969","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) forbade killing a living creature after tying it up."
"6970","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) forbade killing the shrike, the frog, the ant and the hoopoe."
"6971","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) forbade killing the frog for medicine."
"6972","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) forbade killing women and children."
"6973","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) forbade killing any living creature."
"6974","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) forbade the earnings of slave-women (by unlawful means)."
"6975","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) forbade the earnings of a slave-woman until it is known where they came from."
"6976","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) forbade the earnings of the cupper."
"6977","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) forbade every intoxicant."
"6978","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) forbade the milk of the jallalah (an animal that feeds on filth)."
"6979","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) forbade picking up the lost property of the pilgrims."
"6980","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) forbade having intercourse with women through the back passage."
"6981","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) forbade plucking out white hairs."
"6982","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) forbade, in prayer, pecking quickly like a crow, spreading the arms like a predatory animal, and a man making a particular place in the mosque his own, just as a camel makes its place its own."
